                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who works in or supports a certain kind of system of selling and buying, for example free marketeer, black marketeer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f1b8495-de53-4198-9bf2-1f64b7765546",
                        "source_entry_id": "8bba1197-37ec-35c8-b6cf-a44dc3bd4202",
                        "source_sense_id": "af33913e-19db-3f66-bc2f-0a893f482375",
                        "target_lang_word": "huckster",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "huckster",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15969ac3-51ef-33ea-8702-97126fad0b79",
                                        "entry_id": "59e166ed-195e-3358-9596-4defd4cb817d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A peddler or hawker, who sells small items, either door-to-door, from a stall, or in the street."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd7ac31-dac6-4597-86b5-ba94eded280a",
                                                "sense_id": "15969ac3-51ef-33ea-8702-97126fad0b79",
                                                "text": "drive those china hucksters from the doors"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e19c0c0-dd76-3433-ab62-5e7c6bc6915d",
                                        "entry_id": "59e166ed-195e-3358-9596-4defd4cb817d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody who sells things in an aggressive or showy manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2707cd6d-8853-41cb-94d4-5d9cb053c810",
                                                "sense_id": "0e19c0c0-dd76-3433-ab62-5e7c6bc6915d",
                                                "text": "Like most human activities, ballooning has sponsored heroes and hucksters and a good deal in between. For every dedicated scientist patiently recording atmospheric pressure and wind speed while shivering at high altitudes, there is a carnival barker with a bevy of pretty girls willing to dangle from a basket or parachute down to earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1f677b3-9b9d-39d0-a2c6-ddc2e170acf5",
                                        "entry_id": "59e166ed-195e-3358-9596-4defd4cb817d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who deceptively sells fraudulent products; snake oil salesman"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76a0d1b0-b402-34d2-843d-69a9558f8cc8",
                                        "entry_id": "59e166ed-195e-3358-9596-4defd4cb817d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody who writes advertisements for radio or television."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "huckster",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21f81f53-76ff-381b-a0cd-8797318eaeef",
                                        "entry_id": "3922898f-e321-3898-b87e-e557eb70cc9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To haggle, to wrangle, or to bargain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "320f701c-05ac-3026-b00c-45fa938fab47",
                                        "entry_id": "3922898f-e321-3898-b87e-e557eb70cc9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sell or offer (goods) from place to place, to peddle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04903401-3dc6-37f6-9939-9babbfc2794d",
                                        "entry_id": "3922898f-e321-3898-b87e-e557eb70cc9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To promote or sell (goods) in an aggressive, showy manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27bbc758-0453-46e7-b2ff-3974c93dfa87",
                                                "sense_id": "04903401-3dc6-37f6-9939-9babbfc2794d",
                                                "text": "[…] Paul Zindel aroused the hope that he might be a playwright in the Williams mode, one who could cast a kindly light in the dark corners of twisted souls. That is precisely the hope dashed by his latest play, The Secret Affairs of Mildred Wild. Here he is simply huckstering kookdom for cheap laughs, and not producing many of them at that."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfe5b0c0-cd1f-40eb-b870-6474cba2eec8",
                        "source_entry_id": "8bba1197-37ec-35c8-b6cf-a44dc3bd4202",
                        "source_sense_id": "af33913e-19db-3f66-bc2f-0a893f482375",
                        "target_lang_word": "spiv",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spiv",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d3da190-1afd-3609-8e91-25495521b246",
                                        "entry_id": "c6bd88d4-2648-3a07-aa3a-1f99ce70b70f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A smartly dressed person who trades in illicit, black-market or stolen goods, especially during World War II."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "954a706a-b9f7-3966-b95e-ce0300db6321",
                                        "entry_id": "c6bd88d4-2648-3a07-aa3a-1f99ce70b70f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A flashy con artist, often homeless, who lives by his wits."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4b4072-5525-4b60-a06f-d254345f2cb1",
                                                "sense_id": "954a706a-b9f7-3966-b95e-ce0300db6321",
                                                "text": "I mean, Mayfair is just top spivs stepping into the slippers of the former gentry, and Belgravia, like I've said, is all flats in houses built as palaces, and Chelsea—well!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b60a6e8-2a82-4c72-aae8-a37a172f32dc",
                                                "sense_id": "954a706a-b9f7-3966-b95e-ce0300db6321",
                                                "text": "It was Robeson who introduced me to the other blacks in New York, the Show Boat cast, the hangers-on, girlfriends, spivs, and bookies. \"My people,\" he called them, \"my brothers and sisters\" […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2eb0156-4bf9-4ab5-b3fb-d31a72bd6909",
                                                "sense_id": "954a706a-b9f7-3966-b95e-ce0300db6321",
                                                "text": "I make no apology for attacking spivs and gamblers who did more harm to the British economy than [transport union leader] Bob Crow could achieve in his wildest Trotskyite fantasies, while paying themselves outrageous bonuses underwritten by the taxpayer."
                                            }
